# Landlord SMS line — use `phone_number`, not `e164`

`sms_numbers` stores the DID in **`phone_number`**. There is no `e164` column on that table.

## Rule

| API | From-number field |
|---|---|
| `findActiveLandlordMainNumber` → `LandlordSmsNumberRow` | `row.phone_number` via `landlordSmsRowFromNumber(row)` |
| `resolveOutboundLandlordSmsLine` → `OutboundLandlordSmsLine` | `line.phone` (already normalized) |

## Why

Reading `row.e164` is always `undefined`. Call sites then treat the landlord line as missing and **quietly skip** silence nudges, rent reminders, and other outbound SMS (`return false` / `no landlord SMS line` warn) with no hard failure.

## Do

```ts
const line = await findActiveLandlordMainNumber(supabase, landlordId)
const fromNumber = landlordSmsRowFromNumber(line)
if (!fromNumber) { /* skip / error */ }
```

## Do not

```ts
if (!line?.e164) return false
fromNumber: line.e164
```

Incident reference: intake silence follow-ups never sent until the sender switched to `phone_number` (`bf4c6cc`).
